// Radial formation conduction coupled to the two-fluid temperature equation
// (D3 increment 1). Steady single-phase liquid flow through a horizontal pipe
// whose wall is no longer an infinite isothermal reservoir: a finite rock
// mass conducts radially from the bore wall r_w = D/2 = 0.01 m out to a far
// field r_e = 0.2 m held at T_e = 280 K. The formation{} block discretises
// the rock into M = 10 geometric radial nodes rho_j = r_w (r_e/r_w)^(j/M).
//
// Two self-derived anchors (cylindrical Fourier conduction, no transcription):
//  1. The face conductance g_j = 2 pi k dx / ln(rho_{j+1}/rho_j) makes the
//     steady node profile the EXACT logarithm
//       T_j = T_w + (T_e - T_w) ln(rho_j/r_w) / ln(r_e/r_w),
//     which on geometric nodes is LINEAR in j: T_j = T_w + (T_e - T_w) j/M.
//  2. The film (k' dx) and the formation resistance
//     R_form = ln(r_e/r_w)/(2 pi k dx) act in series, so the fluid sees an
//     effective conductance g_eff = 1/(1/(k' dx) + R_form) to T_e and the
//     steady fluid profile is the exchanger recurrence
//       T_i - T_e = (T_in - T_e) r^(i+1),  r = mcd/(mcd + g_eff).
// The rock starts at T_e and stores heat (rhoC > 0); the run is long enough
// (~130 formation time constants) that the storage vanishes and the steady
// anchors hold to 1e-9. The checker also asserts the per-frame formation
// energy balance intake = storage + far-field rejection (exact by construction).
//
// Measured (mcd = 26.2637 W/K, k'dx = 2, R_form = 2.38393 K/W, g_eff = 0.346749):
//   r = 0.986969, r^20 = 0.769247 -> T_out = 318.462 K
//   wall node T_w,i = 280 + (T_i - 280) * 0.826626
//   formation nodes linear in j between T_w and 280
//   qWall = -qFar at steady, qStore -> 0
// D3 increment 2 (5.84) deliberately leaves semiInfinite UNDECLARED here:
// this file is the bit-identical zero-declaration witness (finite Dirichlet
// far field, all 132 increment-1 anchors). The checker derives the
// semiInfinite arms into a system temp dir: a long arm (unbounded rise), a
// 30-step reportEvery-1 arm (Duhamel reconstruction), its Dirichlet twin
// (early-time identity), a geothermal arm (depth profile + shared rise) and
// a scope twin (the word outside formation{} is ignored). E1 is weighed by
// an independent adaptive-Simpson quadrature, never trusted from the app.
// verified by tests/check_two_fluid_formation.py
// (ctest verify.twoFluidFormationRadial, 300 criteria; no new test added).
fluid
{
    rhoL 1000; rhoG 20; muL 0.01; muG 1e-5;
    cL 4180; cG 2150;
}

pipe
{
    length 2; diameter 0.02; roughness 0; angleDeg 0; sections 20;
}

closure
{
    model wallis; slipVelocity 0;
}

initial
{
    alpha 1; temperature 300;
}

boundaries
{
    inlet { type phaseRates; vsl 0.02; vsg 0; temperature 330; }
    outlet { type fixedPressure; p 0; temperature 330; }
}

thermal
{
    wallHeatTransfer 20;
    wallModel constant;
    wallTemperature 280;
}

formation
{
    conductivity 2;
    outerRadius 0.2;
    rhoC 10000;
    shells 10;
}

time { dt 1; endTime 2000; reportEvery 100; }